   "text": "Reading the drawing from left to right gives HS\u2013CH2\u2013CH2\u2013CH(NH2)\u2013COOH, which is homocysteine.\n\n- **Chain:** the thiol (HS) sits on the left. Two CH2 carbons follow, then the central CH carbon, then the carboxylic acid carbon with its C=O and OH.\n- **Stereocentre:** the only wedge is the bold bond from the central carbon to NH2, so that carbon is the only stereocentre drawn. The CIP priorities are N, then COOH, then CH2, with H pointing away from the viewer. Going from N (bottom) to COOH (upper right) to CH2 (upper left) runs counterclockwise, so the centre is S, which is the L-amino-acid configuration.\n- **SMILES check:** `SCC[C@H](N)C(=O)O` lists the neighbours of the stereocentre as CH2, H, N, COOH, and `@` means counterclockwise when viewed from the CH2. This is the same arrangement as the standard L-homocysteine string `N[C@@H](CCS)C(=O)O`, since swapping N and CH2 flips `@@` to `@`.\n\nSMILES: SCC[C@H](N)C(=O)O"
